EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: CoreDNS 1.11.1 enforces a CNAME-chain depth limit — assumption A1 is refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: coredns/coredns:1.11.1
TARGET_PORT: 53/udp
CLIENT_TOOL: scapy

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent 1,000 concurrent DNS queries referencing crafted CNAME chains of depth 100+.
  CoreDNS returned SERVFAIL for every query after reaching its depth limit (10 hops).
  CPU spiked briefly to ~12% then returned to <2%. Memory delta < 5 MB. No goroutine
  accumulation observed in /debug/vars. The depth guard in plugin/pkg/dnsutil
  terminates recursion before significant allocation occurs.
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("no depth bound") is refuted. The CNAME depth limit
                has been present in CoreDNS since v1.4.0.
